    "payload": {
      "feedback": "The deliverable is a solid start \u2013 it captures a clear value proposition, three well\u2011defined personas, a prioritized feature list, and concise user stories. However, it falls short of being fully specific, complete, and actionable for development:\n\n1. **Missing Acceptance Criteria** \u2013 Each user story should include concrete acceptance criteria (Given/When/Then) to guide testing and verification.\n\n2. **Technical Detail Gaps** \u2013 No information on platform (iOS/Android), tech stack, API contracts, data model schemas, or integration specifics (e.g., OAuth, webhook formats for VetSync).\n\n3. **Non\u2011functional Requirements** \u2013 No coverage of performance (latency targets for the real\u2011time feed), scalability (how many concurrent users/clinics), security compliance (HIPAA, GDPR), offline support, or accessibility.\n\n4. **MVP Scope & Phasing** \u2013 It\u2019s unclear which features constitute the minimum viable product versus later phases; a release roadmap or priority matrix would make it actionable.\n\n5. **UX/UI Guidance** \u2013 No wireframes, screen flow, or UI/UX guidelines (e.g., how the location search UI behaves, booking confirmation design).\n\n6. **Metrics & Success Criteria** \u2013 Lacks measurable KPIs (e.g., average time to book, fill\u2011rate of empty slots, user retention) to evaluate whether the product meets its goals.\n\n7. **Operational Considerations** \u2013 No mention of monitoring, logging, error\u2011handling strategy for API failures, or a fallback when real\u2011time availability is unavailable beyond a banner.\n\n8. **Legal/Compliance Details** \u2013 While vet verification is noted, the process for ongoing license renewal checks, data retention policies, and user consent flows are absent.\n\nTo make the output actionable, enrich it with the above elements. As it stands, the work is incomplete for hand\u2011off to engineering and product teams.",
      "idea": "A mobile app that helps dog owners find nearby vets with real-time availability",
      "focus": "Define user personas (dog owners, vets), outline core features (location-based search, real-time availability, appointment booking, reviews, push notifications), create wireframes and user journey maps for the mobile app, specify vet verification process and data privacy requirements, and draft a product requirement document with MVP scope."
    },
    "timestamp": "2026-04-21T08:38:33.934203+00:00",
    "parent_message_id": "msg-fc88b494"
